WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER

The licence above covers the source code. It does not cover the contents of
`backend/public/` — the audio guides, the photographs and the narration text —
which are the material the product sells and are not offered under it.

That distinction is not boilerplate. It is here because the two things have
genuinely different owners:

  - the narration text was written for this project and its Italian originals
    are the author's, but the translations into five languages and every audio
    track were produced by a model (gpt-4o-mini and gpt-4o-mini-tts);

  - the photographs are the part that went wrong once, and the record is kept
    in `docs/immagini.md` rather than hidden. Twenty-four images turned out to
    carry other photographers' copyright in their metadata and have been
    replaced. Anything added from here on has to have a known source, and
    `credits` in the POI record is where it goes.

If you are reading this in order to reuse something: the code, freely. The
guides, no — ask.
